course: dictionary
lesson: 13136
title: Forbidding: scary or saying no
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Forbidding» has two jobs, so read the words around it to find out which one it has. In «The forbidding mountains loomed above the village», the mountains look unfriendly and frightening, so you would not want to go near them.
explain: The second job is when forbidding is the -ing form of forbid. Forbid means telling someone they must not do something. In «The sign was forbidding people from swimming», the sign is saying no. Ask yourself: is someone saying no? If so, it is the verb.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Frightening mountains» still makes sense, so the first meaning fits. «The sign was telling people they must not swim» also makes sense, so the second meaning fits.
fact: Forbidding is an adjective when it describes how something looks or feels: a forbidding castle.
fact: «Forbidding» means looking unfriendly, frightening or dangerous.
fact: Forbid is a verb meaning to tell someone that they must not do something.
fact: The verb forms are forbid, forbids, forbade, forbidden and forbidding.
fact: Context clues help: in a scary story, forbidding sets the mood, while on a sign or in a rule, it means no.
exercise: «The forbidding castle stood alone on the cliff.» What does forbidding mean here? | Full of food | *Looking unfriendly and frightening | Very friendly and welcoming | Painted bright red
exercise: «The sign at the pool was forbidding children from running.» What is the sign doing? | Making the pool deeper | *Telling children they must not run | Inviting children to run races | Showing a picture of a tall castle
exercise: Find the word in «The forbidding sky looked dark and stormy» that describes how the sky looks. | sky | looked | stormy | *forbidding
test: «Mum is forbidding us from having sweets before dinner.» What does forbidding mean here? | Giving us lots of sweets | Hiding the sweets in a cupboard | Telling us we can have sweets now | *Telling us we must not have sweets
test: Forbidding is the -ing form of which word? | forget | *forbid | forgive | frighten
exam: In «The forbidding mountains had a sign forbidding climbing», which forbidding means telling people they must not do something? | Neither of them | The first one | Both of them | *The second one
